    <title>Daily Digest 2026-08-27: Show HN: I built an agent-first productivity bridg; LLM-Based Social Engineering Scams; Show HN: Reconstruct distributed LLM training trac</title>
    <updated>2026-08-27T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-08-27.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: I built an agent-first productivity bridge for all your agents&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://www.taskshell.app/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;LLM-Based Social Engineering Scams&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://www.schneier.com/blog/archives/2026/08/llm-based-social-engineering-scams.html"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Reconstruct distributed LLM training traces&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://trace.vladsavinov.com/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Kubernetes v1.37: Garhwal&lt;/b&gt; — Kubernetes ecosystem changes can surface new operational patterns or affect your existing clusters. &lt;a href="https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Contextual – local codebase memory for AI coding agents&lt;/b&gt; — Community-vetted signal from Hacker News — high upvote-to-age ratio means the engineering community found it worth reading. &lt;a href="https://contextuallabs.dev"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Qwen3.8-Flash-Next&lt;/b&gt; — Design patterns and lessons from production systems — high-leverage reading for senior engineers. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/26/qwen38-flash-next/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;TypeScript 7 and What Comes Next&lt;/b&gt; — New release or open-sourced project — quick scan to see if it belongs in your toolkit. &lt;a href="https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/podcasts/typescript-7-and-what-comes-next/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;#501 – DHH: Future of Programming, AI, Agentic Engineering, Vibe Coding &amp;amp; Linux&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://lexfridman.com/dhh-2/?utm_source=rss&amp;amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;amp;utm_campaign=dhh-2"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;A polymorphic phishing page (that occasionally breaks itself), (Thu, Aug 27th)&lt;/b&gt; — Flagged as relevant to your interests — read the summary to decide if it's worth your time. &lt;a href="https://isc.sans.edu/diary/rss/33290"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
